<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>What should a daily commuter check on a rental motorbike in Hanoi?</h2>
<p>The honest routine is small, the daily glance at the first mount, the tyres, the lights, the brakes&rsquo; first answer and anything new the machine is wearing, and the weekly look on an anchored quiet hour, the chain&rsquo;s voice, the cables, the fastenings and the storage&rsquo;s dryness, with every change worth a sentence at the counter. The routine&rsquo;s total cost is minutes a week, and it is the rider&rsquo;s entire share of the shared care a hundred commuting mornings ride on.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>Does heavy daily riding change the rental&rsquo;s maintenance terms in Hanoi?</h2>
<p>The terms themselves are the shop&rsquo;s practice and the same to every asker, but the honest commuter describes the heavy month at the rental sitting, because the arrangement is stated with the use in mind and a machine ridden a hundred times reads differently in the care conversation than one ridden twenty. What the rental includes by way of servicing, and the procedure for the odd morning, are asked once at the desk, in daylight, before the first commute begins.</p>
